  "summary": "Standard optical and electron microscopes cannot measure mechanical stiffness directly. To measure the bulk stiffness (storage modulus) of a soft hydrogel, hybrid rheometers EQ21 and EQ19 are available. If you specifically require spatially resolved, microscopic stiffness mapping, an atomic force microscope (AFM) with indentation capability would be required but is not currently listed."
}

{
  "measurement_needs": [
    "Melting temperature (Tm) and melting onset",
    "Heat of fusion (enthalpy of melting) and degree of crystallinity",
