      "why_useful": "Provides non-contact, quantitative 3D areal surface roughness measurements, although lateral resolution may be limited compared to AFM at a 5 × 5 µm scan scale."
    }
  ],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "No listed instrument can perform the quantitative nanoscale RMS surface roughness measurement you need for a 5 × 5 µm area. Atomic Force Microscopy (AFM) is the appropriate technique for this measurement but is not present on the equipment list. The Philips XL30 ESEM (EQ10) can serve as a supplementary tool to qualitatively inspect nanoscale surface textures."
}

{
  "measurement_needs": [
    "Recovery force or blocking stress generated by shape memory polymers during constrained thermal activation",
    "Thermal transition / activation temperature (glass transition or melting point)"
  ],
  "objective_met": true,
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ21",
      "role": "primary",
      "technique": "Thermomechanical / normal force testing under controlled temperature ramp",
      "why": "With its confirmed Environmental Test Chamber (ETC), the HR20 can apply a fixed strain to a programmed sample and record the normal/axial recovery force (up to 50 N) as the chamber heats past the activation temperature.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Solid tension or compression geometries (such as solid rectangular/film tension clamps or parallel plates compatible with the ETC)",
        "Sub-ambient cooling system (if activation occurs below or near ambient temperature)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ15",
      "role": "primary",
      "technique": "Constrained (isometric) recovery force testing via universal mechanical testing",
      "why": "A universal testing machine can measure high recovery forces generated during shape recovery while holding the deformed sample at fixed displacement during activation.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Environmental / temperature chamber or fluid heating bath to activate the specimen",
        "Appropriately sized load cell",
        "Tensile grips or compression platens rated for the test temperature"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ18",
      "role": "supplementary",
      "technique": "Differential scanning calorimetry (DSC)",
      "why": "Accurately determines the thermal transition temperature (glass transition temperature or melting temperature) that triggers the shape memory recovery.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "Standard Tzero aluminum pans and hermetic lids"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "not_available": [
